{"title":"2012 CIMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 Part D","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.5</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\" title=\"2012 CIMC Problems/Part B Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rowan is given a square grid whose side length is an odd integer. The square is then divided into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> squares,. Rowan shades each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> square along the two diagonals and does not shade any of the remaining squares. For example, a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> grid is shown in which Rowan has shaded the squares along the diagonals.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_D&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_D&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rowan is given a fourth square grid with odd side length. After shading the squares on the diagonals, there are 196 <i>unshaded</i> 1 by 1 squares. How many 1 by 1 squares does this grid contain in total?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_D&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that the number of shaded squares for a square grid is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/f/03f5a5ded7724c11e58ef212dc3e8549071890a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a whole number representing the number of rows and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/4/c2431d0a48a98e17dd97849781d5c3c9ff4911a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\neq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" /> because there would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> squares for each diagonal, except the center square is repeated twice. \n</p><p>Since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/f/c5f40cb7585c44d066022164abae4d42af57a926.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$196$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> unshaded squares and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> rows and columns, there would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec8c0bb5d2961b165a48f63a50499121cc169f0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^{2} - 196$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> shaded squares. We then have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/c/f3c3ee42590f6c07a2b19fb05ca669d7ed17556f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^{2} - 196 = 2n - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/e/8fe5a7cdac5b7cde38837a0051ea9233a75f875d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^{2} - 2n - 195 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/6/d06eecef0b7885fd1743e80c0d82ac1327b5be68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^{2} - 15n + 13n - 195 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"206\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/a/04a4402c5664d041a7639fb2abcb1eb84af15b90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(n - 15) + 13(n - 15) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"217\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/5/92543c09b9b87ad5bd527ed35cb87394a3ce03a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n + 13)(n - 15) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must be positive, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/a/d5a242689b4cdcd8be0c39edc9a19ed508070de3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, the total number of squares is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/c/5fc0152f9903ae49defe8aa062d68f33ef529621.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15^{2} = \\boxed{225}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"90\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.5\">Solution 1.5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_D&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like in solution 1, we can get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/c/f3c3ee42590f6c07a2b19fb05ca669d7ed17556f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^{2} - 196 = 2n - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>This gives:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/0/5c03fddb00ac319f141d85e680d91d1c9b94dd48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^{2} - 2n + 1 = 196$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/d/36d5f34b104614805aef4fb05229b04e1844cc3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n - 1)^{2} = 196$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is positive, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/f/3ff118c1537456811b40a86042e32bc0c56c8107.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n - 1 = \\sqrt{196} = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"153\" height=\"21\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/a/d5a242689b4cdcd8be0c39edc9a19ed508070de3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, the total number of squares is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/c/5fc0152f9903ae49defe8aa062d68f33ef529621.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15^{2} = \\boxed{225}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"90\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018055302\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.041 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 133/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1299/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5050/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.585      1 2012_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\n100.00%   13.585      1 -total\n 40.17%    5.457      1 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37086:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018055302 and revision id 286391. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}